From: nobrega8 <afonsognobrega@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:34:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] XSNium: lay text lines out in whole pixels, as IE does

Internet Explorer lays out InfoPath forms in whole pixels at 96 DPI,
with GDI's line metrics: the font's OS/2 win ascent and descent, no
leading, the font's size rounded to pixels and then the ascent and
descent. Writer's metrics make each line a fraction of a pixel taller
or shorter (Calibri 9pt: 14.67px against IE's 14px), and a form drifts
from its design by several pixels.

The PixelLineMetrics document setting (off by default) makes Writer
measure lines that way. vcl::font::GetWinLineMetrics gives the win
ascent and descent, which VCL's FontMetric does not expose.

Change-Id: Ic0e1b6887facedb49fedcfcfc0d2994b41755645
